-- title:
--   Descent of integrality over K[jmatĥ] along σ: K→ℂ
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure, $\sigma\colon K\to\mathbb{C}$ a ring homomorphism, $N\ge 1$ an integer, $m$ a natural number and $f$ a modular form of weight $2m$ for $\Gamma_0(N)$. Write $\hat\jmath_L =$ `coeffEmb L jq` for the image in $L((q))$ of the Laurent series $jq = q^{-1}\cdot jNumQ(q)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ (the $q$-expansion of the modular invariant, $jNumQ$ being the rational power series `jNum`) under the coefficientwise map induced by $\mathbb{Q}\to L$, and let $\theta$ denote the $\mathbb{C}$-linear operator `thetaL` on $\mathbb{C}((q))$ sending $g$ to $q\,g'$. Suppose $y\in K((q))$ satisfies $$\sigma_*(y)\cdot\bigl(\theta\,\hat\jmath_{\mathbb{C}}\bigr)^m = \hat f,$$ where $\sigma_*$ is the coefficientwise map $K((q))\to\mathbb{C}((q))$ induced by $\sigma$ and $\hat f$ is the Laurent series attached to the $q$-expansion `qExpansion 1 f` of $f$ (width $1$). Then $$y^6\,\hat\jmath_K^{\,4m}\,(\hat\jmath_K-1728)^{3m}\in K((q))$$ is integral over the $K$-subalgebra $K[\hat\jmath_K]$ of $K((q))$ generated by $\hat\jmath_K$, where $1728$ is understood via the structure map $K\to K((q))$.
--
--   This is the descent to coefficients in an arbitrary $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra field $K$ of the integrality, over the subalgebra generated by the $q$-expansion of $j$, of the $q$-expansion of a weight-$2m$ form on $\Gamma_0(N)$ after clearing the poles of $\theta j$ at the elliptic points and the cusp. It is used in the construction of mod-$p$ forms and mod-$p$ cusp forms from characteristic-zero $q$-expansions, where $K$ is taken to be a field such as $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ together with a chosen complex embedding.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_isIntegral_adjoin_coeffEmb_jq_of_coeffMap_mul_thetaL_pow_eq_qExpansion.lean

